"""Render reviewed capacity receipts as a human-readable report; no pipeline orchestration."""
import json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).parent;data=json.loads((r/'tests/measurements/capacity-results.json').read_text())
text='''# Complete pipeline feedback and runner capacity\n\n## Scope and evidence\n\n[PBI-086](../../BACKLOG.md#pbi-086-measure-complete-pipeline-feedback-and-runner-capacity) requires the complete JDK, SQLcl, utPLSQL and Oracle workload. The [design](sprint_E.18_design.md) defines this Elaboration experiment. Every admitted sample runs the existing five backend cases and complete E.17 native delivery, refusal, authenticated APEX/ORDS and cleanup checks. [Verification](sprint_E.18_tests.md) records gates; [raw measurements](tests/measurements/capacity-results.json) contain individual samples and phase times. Failed and exploratory trials are excluded, retained in the [bug record](sprint_E.18_bugs.md).\n\nTwo successful replicas per comparison cell yield eight observations. The initial warm population run is excluded. Median is the sample median; p95 uses nearest rank and equals the maximum at n=2. No production tail estimate is implied. All times below are seconds, with API timestamp resolution of one second. Cache warmth covers checksum-verified SQLcl/APEX archive downloads only; Oracle image pulls, fresh databases, native validation and backend execution remain in every job.\n'''
for k,v in data['groups'].items():
 samples=[s for s in data['samples'] if f"{s['cache']}-parallel-{s['parallel']}"==k]
 text+='\n## '+k+'\n\n'
 for metric,title in [('execution_seconds','Execution'),('feedback_seconds','Workflow-to-completion feedback'),('queue_seconds','Total admission and queue')]:
  d=v[metric];text+=f"{title}: n={d['n']}, median {d['median']:.1f}, nearest-rank p95 {d['p95']:.1f} seconds.\n\n"
 text+=f"Observed host used-memory peak range {min(s['peak_host_used_bytes'] for s in samples)/2**30:.2f}–{max(s['peak_host_used_bytes'] for s in samples)/2**30:.2f} GiB. Minimum observed free root disk {min(s['minimum_disk_free_bytes'] for s in samples)/2**30:.2f} GiB. Mean host CPU busy across each sample ranges {min(s['host_cpu_busy_percent'] for s in samples):.1f}–{max(s['host_cpu_busy_percent'] for s in samples):.1f}%. These include background runner demand.\n\n"
 text+='Individual scheduling decomposition: '+ '; '.join(f"replica {s['replica']}: scheduler queue {s['scheduler_queue_seconds']:.1f}s; admission {s['admission_seconds']:.1f}s; {s['resource_samples']} resource observations" for s in samples)+'.\n\n'
 text+='Recorded tool/hardware inputs: '+ '; '.join(f"replica {s['replica']}: JDK {', '.join(s['jdk_builds'])}, SQLcl {s['sqlcl_build']}, processor {s['cpu_model']}" for s in samples)+'. utPLSQL source is pinned to 072dfbc1d0ed37f8da9c0ff87823906483ea3887; Oracle and ORDS image digests are retained in the workflow and job logs.\n\n'
 text+='### Phase timings\n\nEach line reports median and observed range across the two replicas. Setup/checkout/post phases are retained where GitHub reports success.\n\n'
 names=list(samples[0]['phases'])
 for name in names:
  values=[s['phases'][name] for s in samples if name in s['phases']]
  text+=f"- {name}: median {statistics.median(values):.1f}s; range {min(values):.1f}–{max(values):.1f}s.\n"
text+='\n## Observed comparisons\n\n'
for mode in ['cold','warm']:
 serial=data['groups'][mode+'-parallel-1']['feedback_seconds']['p95'];concurrent=data['groups'][mode+'-parallel-2']['feedback_seconds']['p95']
 text+=f"{mode.title()} two-job batch completion: one slot {serial:.1f}s, two slots {concurrent:.1f}s; observed ratio {serial/concurrent:.2f}. This includes admission/queue and uses the slowest completion in each two-job batch.\n\n"
for parallel in [1,2]:
 cold=[s for s in data['samples'] if s['cache']=='cold' and s['parallel']==parallel];warm=[s for s in data['samples'] if s['cache']=='warm' and s['parallel']==parallel]
 names=['Install qualified SQLcl','Acquire checksum pinned APEX']
 c=statistics.median(sum(s['phases'][n] for n in names) for s in cold);w=statistics.median(sum(s['phases'][n] for n in names) for s in warm)
 text+=f"At parallel {parallel}, combined SQLcl/APEX acquisition phase median is cold {c:.1f}s versus warm {w:.1f}s (difference {c-w:.1f}s). Cache restore/save overhead is listed separately in phase timings; hardware/network/time variation prevents a causal speedup claim.\n\n"
text+='''\n## Capacity and caching recommendation\n\nUse one independent ephemeral runner per complete workload, retaining fresh author/target databases and all validation. For a two-candidate batch, provision two such slots when shorter batch feedback is worth two simultaneous runner allocations. Serial execution remains an option when cost or admission limits dominate. The observed serial/concurrent feedback and resource values above establish this bounded tradeoff, not a measured shared-host packing limit. Do not place two complete database workloads on one host based on these independent-host results.\n\nRetain the measured hosted runner shape as the qualified starting capacity; inspect each sample's cpu.txt and memory-start.txt for exact processor and memory observations. Keep the explicit disposable-host disk preparation: the original E.17 worker exhausted disk without it. Preserve measured free-disk margin rather than treating remaining free bytes as a safe reduction. Archive caching is safe only with checksum revalidation and unchanged native checks. Compare the measured download-phase savings against restore/save overhead before adopting it; full APEX installation can dominate overall feedback even when download time falls. No claim of cache speedup is made unless the actual paired phase measurements support it.\n\n## Measurement limits\n\nThe workload is the bounded laboratory release and five-case backend suite, not a production application load test. Hosted hardware, network and image prepopulation may vary. Trials at different times do not isolate cache as the sole cause of elapsed-time differences. Host CPU counters and available memory are sampled every five seconds; short peaks and process attribution are unmeasured. Queue decomposition uses GitHub job/workflow creation and start times, so any unexposed platform delay remains folded into those values. Serial admission is part of feedback, not application execution. Larger repeated samples and representative production datasets are needed before service-level or shared-host sizing commitments. Mandatory validation and isolation remain unchanged.\n'''
(r/'capacity_report.md').write_text(text)
